# ChatGPT Scratchpad

Last updated: 2026-05-25

Purpose: This is the working handoff between ChatGPT, Chad, Codex, and ongoing design/product thinking around Nova Notetaker. Keep this file current with design direction, UX decisions, workflow concerns, branding guidance, UI review notes, product recommendations, and unresolved design questions.

## Current Design Perspective

Nova Notetaker is evolving beyond a simple meeting recorder.

The strongest emerging product identity is:

- Passive AI meeting intelligence for enterprise users.

Nova currently feels differentiated because it is:

- Native Windows desktop software.
- Local-first in workflow.
- Self-hosted AI friendly.
- Privacy-conscious.
- Passive rather than invasive.

Nova is NOT positioning itself as:

- A Teams bot.
- A cloud-only transcription SaaS.
- Another Copilot clone.
- A browser-first AI utility.

Current architecture decisions reinforce the product identity well:

- WASAPI loopback capture.
- Optional microphone capture.
- Self-hosted WhisperLive.
- Self-hosted Ollama.
- Internal infrastructure.
- Local meeting storage.

